Third-party components

This application bundles and depends on third-party software and data that
remain subject to their own licenses, including (non-exhaustively):

  - Kotlin, Compose Multiplatform, SQLDelight, Coil, AndroidX, kaml,
    osmdroid, TensorFlow Lite (LiteRT): Apache License 2.0
  - AIY Birds V1 photo model, © Google: Apache License 2.0
  - BirdNET-Lite sound model, K. Lisa Yang Center for Conservation
    Bioacoustics, Cornell Lab of Ornithology, Cornell University:
    CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  - DM Serif Display, Caveat: SIL Open Font License 1.1
  - Species photos from Wikimedia Commons: CC0, public domain, CC BY or
    CC BY-SA, as recorded for each photo
  - Species selection and English names: BirdLife Sweden's taxonomic
    committee, Western Palearctic list (VP11), checked against the IOC
    World Bird List (F. Gill, D. Donsker & P. Rasmussen, eds.; CC BY 3.0)
  - Swedish names: mostly Wikidata (CC0), some from BirdLife Sweden's
    official list; red-list categories (IUCN): Wikidata (CC0)
  - Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL); map tiles © MapTiler

These third-party licenses govern their respective components and are not
affected by the proprietary terms above. The app shows the credits for photos,
texts, models and libraries under Settings → About.

Species texts (exception to the proprietary terms above)

The species texts, that is the `description` and `migration` fields of the
species files in shared/content/species/ and the same texts in the app's
species database, are summaries that an AI model wrote from Wikipedia articles.
They are adaptations of Wikipedia text and are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The Wikipedia article
revisions they are based on are listed in the `sources` field of each species
file.

Species pages on the website (exception to the proprietary terms above)

The species texts in website/src/data/species/ and the comparison texts in
website/src/data/comparisons/ are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0, see the LICENSE.md
file in each folder. Photos and recordings in website/src/assets/species/ keep the
licenses credited in the species files and on each page.
